&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of successful sales experience in hematology/oncology, molecular diagnostics, surgical oncology, or a closely related healthcare field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of meeting or exceeding sales goals, developing new business, and growing complex territories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of academic and community oncology markets, clinical workflows, precision medicine, and reimbursement dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging hematologists, medical oncologists, pathologists, and other oncology decision-makers strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of lymphoma, hematologic malignancies, and molecular diagnostic testing highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel approximately 50–75% throughout the assigned territory.&lt;/li&gt;
