&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Business Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify growth opportunities, develop account-specific strategies, and coordinate internal resources to achieve organizational objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; Market Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a comprehensive understanding of Natera&#39;s technology, testing solutions, and competitive landscape to effectively represent the organization at the executive level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Travel up to 70% to support customer relationships, strategic initiatives, and internal collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience required; MBA preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 3 years of physician-facing sales experience in the diagnostic laboratory industry, preferably molecular diagnostics or genetics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 3 years of successful strategic account management, key account sales, or consultative selling experience, preferably within diagnostics or healthcare.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in expanding strategic accounts, developing new markets, launching products, and driving revenue growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of sales achievement, with recognition for exceptional performance preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating complex hospital systems and IDNs, including EMR integrations, enterprise contracting, and healthcare system decision-making processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established ability to influence senior-level stakeholders, manage complex sales cycles, and build collaborative partnerships across multiple departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic thinking and business acumen, with the ability to translate enterprise objectives into actionable plans.&lt;/li&gt;
