&lt;p&gt;Link: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.natera.com/notice-of-data-collection-california-residents&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://www.natera.com/notice-of-data-collection-california-residents/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please be advised that Natera will reach out to candidates with a @&lt;a href=&quot;http://natera.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=http://natera.com&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1657718972773000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw3zRwaIiu7070kJKNG4hjRm&quot;&gt;natera.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;email domain ONLY. Email communications from all other domain names are not from Natera or its employees and are fraudulent. Natera does not request interviews via text messages and does not ask for personal information until a candidate has engaged with the company and has spoken to a recruiter and the hiring team. Natera takes cyber crimes seriously, and will collaborate with law enforcement authorities to prosecute any related cyber crimes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information:&lt;br&gt;- &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bbb.org/article/tips/12261-bbb-tip-employment-scams&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;BBB announcement on job scams&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;- &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fbi.gov/investigate/cyber&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;FBI Cyber Crime resource page&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #1a1a18;&quot;&gt;The Mobile Patient Services Specialist (MPSS) plays a vital role in ensuring a seamless, patient-centered testing experience in a mobile, field-based setting. Unlike clinic-based coordinators, the MPSS operates independently across a defined service area, traveling directly to patients to perform blood draws, manage specimen logistics, and coordinate care with internal teams, local lab resources, and vendor partners.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #1a1a18;&quot;&gt;This position is responsible for proactively managing patient outreach, scheduling blood draws within required timelines, ensuring specimen integrity, and maintaining accurate documentation across all systems. The ideal candidate is highly organized, self-directed, and comfortable navigating complex logistics with minimal supervision.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a mobile, field-based position serving patients within a defined geographic service area.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #1a1a18;&quot;&gt;Job offer is contingent upon pre-employment requirements and compliance with all applicable regulations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a mobile position based in San Antonio, TX&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Looking at everything we&#39;ve worked on, here&#39;s how it all maps to your layout:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PHLEBOTOMY SERVICES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Perform venipunctures to obtain blood specimens with precision and care.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Verify patient identity and test requisitions, ensuring accuracy by cross-referencing EMR records and resolving discrepancies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Maintain specimen integrity by following aseptic techniques, department protocols, and isolation procedures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Accurately track collected specimens by documenting initials, date, and collection time, while maintaining daily collection logs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PATIENT CARE COORDINATION:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Oversee and coordinate patient care services to ensure efficient and high-quality healthcare delivery.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Contact patients promptly upon order receipt to schedule blood draws within required timeframes, making documented contact attempts and escalating appropriately if no response is received.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Arrange phlebotomy support for out-of-radius patients through appropriate resources, confirming scheduling and ensuring all necessary kits are in place prior to the appointment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Redirect patients who decline MPSS draws to appropriate alternatives, including local labs, Natera PSC locations, or their clinic; utilize self-scheduling platforms where available.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with field sales and internal operations teams to provide patient support and ensure continuity of care.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Develop and maintain strong patient relationships to encourage ongoing testing and adherence to recommended care plans.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADMINISTRATIVE AND OPERATIONAL MANAGEMENT:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Serve as the primary liaison between patients, clinic accounts, Territory Managers, and internal operations teams, documenting all interactions, scheduling actions, and follow-ups in applicable systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Monitor the portal regularly for new orders, verifying completeness and accuracy by cross-referencing source documentation and resolving discrepancies prior to patient contact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Coordinate kit shipment to designated labs following each draw, track receipt through available tools, and escalate any unconfirmed receipts to management for review.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Document and submit specimen photos and update all relevant notations within required timeframes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Respond promptly to internal and external inquiries, proactively communicating delays, cancellations, or redraw needs to relevant stakeholders.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Investigate and resolve escalated issues, providing clear root cause explanations through phone and electronic communication.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALITY ASSURANCE AND COMPLIANCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Serve as the primary compliance owner for all field-based operations, maintaining strict adherence to CAP/CLIA standards and applicable federal, state, and local healthcare regulations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Act as the accountable steward of the mobile workspace, including the assigned vehicle, onboard equipment, specimen storage, and supplies, ensuring all elements consistently meet regulatory, safety, and cleanliness standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Conduct routine self-audits covering temperature logs, equipment calibration, supply expiration, and chain-of-custody documentation, resolving or escalating deficiencies proactively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Coordinate scheduled vehicle maintenance, document mileage and operational readiness, and promptly report mechanical or safety concerns to ensure uninterrupted service delivery.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Execute department protocols and testing schedules with consistency, ensuring all outcomes and corrective actions are accurately recorded and audit-ready.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Identify and escalate compliance risks proactively, taking full ownership of corrective action follow-through.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Monitor field workflows for improvement opportunities, presenting findings and recommendations to leadership to enhance efficiency, accuracy, and patient safety.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Contribute to the development and refinement of mobile phlebotomy SOPs, informed by direct field experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Maintain current certifications, training records, and equipment qualifications, initiating renewals proactively ahead of expiration.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Ensure full compliance with all state and local regulations governing the transport of biohazardous specimens, including proper packaging, labeling, containment, and documentation requirements throughout transit.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #262626 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #262626;&quot;&gt;Minimum of 5 years of phlebotomy experience; 5+ years of Mobile phlebotomy experience &lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #262626 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #262626;&quot;&gt;5+ years high-level customer care experience Managing/supervising phlebotomy operations and teams experience preferred BS/BA degree (preferred)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #262626 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #262626;&quot;&gt;High School Diploma (or equivalent) required Phlebotomy Certification (or equivalent) preferred, except where regulatory regulations are mandated depending upon state&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #262626 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #262626;&quot;&gt;Previous financial and budgetary experience preferred&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #262626 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #262626;&quot;&gt;Bilingual language skills preferred&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Serve and protect the Natera clinic community by adhering to professional standards, hospital policies and procedures, federal, state, and local requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Strong ability to uphold Natera’s professional standards, policies, and regulatory requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Excellent communication, problem-solving, and multitasking skills.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with internal teams and patients.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PHYSICAL DEMANDS AND WORK ENVIRONMENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Office-based and mobile clinic settings; scrubs required with adherence to safe clinical practices for all blood draws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;The majority of time will be spent performing mobile draws across an assigned geographic area. When no mobile draws are scheduled, the employee will report to their assigned Patient Service Center.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Work schedule is determined based on local need&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Must be able to safely lift, carry, and move items weighing up to 50 pounds on a regular basis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUR OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Natera™ is a global leader in cell-free DNA (cfDNA) testing, dedicated to oncology, women’s health, and organ health. Our aim is to make personalized genetic testing and diagnostics part of the standard of care to protect health and enable earlier and more targeted interventions that lead to longer, healthier lives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Natera team consists of highly dedicated statisticians, geneticists, doctors, laboratory scientists, business professionals, software engineers and many other professionals from world-class institutions, who care deeply for our work and each other. When you join Natera, you’ll work hard and grow quickly. Working alongside the elite of the industry, you’ll be stretched and challenged, and take pride in being part of a company that is changing the landscape of genetic disease management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Competitive Benefits - Employee benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life and disability plans for eligible employees and their dependents. Additionally, Natera employees and their immediate families receive free testing in addition to fertility care benefits. Other benefits include pregnancy and baby bonding leave, 401k benefits, commuter benefits and much more. We also offer a generous employee referral program!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.natera.com/&quot; data-cke-saved-href=&quot;http://www.natera.com/&quot;&gt;www.natera.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Natera is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to ensuring a diverse and inclusive workplace environment, and welcome people of different backgrounds, experiences, abilities and perspectives. Inclusive collaboration benefits our employees, our community and our patients, and is critical to our mission of changing the management of disease worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will be considered without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, age, veteran status, disability or any other legally protected status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you are based in California, we encourage you to read this important information for California residents.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Link: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.natera.com/notice-of-data-collection-california-residents&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://www.natera.com/notice-of-data-collection-california-residents/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please be advised that Natera will reach out to candidates with a @&lt;a href=&quot;http://natera.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=http://natera.com&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1657718972773000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw3zRwaIiu7070kJKNG4hjRm&quot;&gt;natera.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;email domain ONLY. Email communications from all other domain names are not from Natera or its employees and are fraudulent. Natera does not request interviews via text messages and does not ask for personal information until a candidate has engaged with the company and has spoken to a recruiter and the hiring team. Natera takes cyber crimes seriously, and will collaborate with law enforcement authorities to prosecute any related cyber crimes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information:&lt;br&gt;- &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bbb.org/article/tips/12261-bbb-tip-employment-scams&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;BBB announcement on job scams&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;- &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fbi.gov/investigate/cyber&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;FBI Cyber Crime resource page&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Oncology Clinical Data Abstractor (Contract, Remote)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Natera, the &lt;strong&gt;Oncology Clinical Data Abstractor&lt;/strong&gt; (fully remote, contract position) will leverage their oncology clinical knowledge and expertise to curate, abstract, and interpret Signatera patient data that is critical for reimbursement. As a clinical expert working within Natera’s AI-enabled platform, you will own the process from initial record review through submission of high-quality, structured data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will rely on your understanding of the oncology patient journey and cancer staging to turn complex clinical records into accurate, reimbursement-ready data. You will work closely with your team to ensure consistency and quality across every record. This role is ideal for a detail-driven oncology nurse who enjoys untangling complex clinical records and takes pride in getting every data point right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical Data Abstraction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Review clinical documentation to abstract key oncology data related to billing and reimbursement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Abstract and interpret stage of disease using AJCC staging guidelines across all tumor types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Ensure accurate, complete, and timely submission of curated data, identifying and communicating patient data deficiencies and discrepancies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Enabled Platform Workflows&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Operationalize outputs from Natera’s AI-enabled platform to manage a daily queue of records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Perform high quality review of AI-generated abstractions, correcting errors and escalating issues as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Validate, finalize, and submit abstracted records within the platform, adapting to new data measures and workflows as they are introduced.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Apply meticulous attention to detail to catch errors, inconsistencies, and gaps before records are submitted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Use critical thinking to interpret complex clinical documentation, resolve ambiguities, and communicate findings clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Manage a high-volume daily queue with strong organization and follow-through, meeting quality and turnaround expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Licensure:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;BSN or higher degree&lt;/strong&gt; required; &lt;strong&gt;MSN preferred&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Current, active &lt;strong&gt;Registered Nurse (RN)&lt;/strong&gt; licensure (state or compact).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;◦ &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Must maintain licensure in good standing throughout the contract term.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;◦ &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt; Board Certification as an &lt;strong&gt;Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Minimum 3 years of oncology clinical experience&lt;/strong&gt; (5+ years preferred) in an inpatient or outpatient setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Detailed understanding of the oncology patient journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Must have:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong knowledge and interpretation of AJCC staging for all tumor types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Solid understanding of cancer biology, pathology, and oncologic treatment modalities in the neoadjuvant and adjuvant settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Technology Adoption:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to master Natera’s AI-enabled platform and other internal platforms as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Systems Familiarity:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with electronic medical records. &lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt; Epic experience, as occasional use is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Collaboration Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; Working knowledge of the Google suite (e.g., Calendar, Chat, Sheets) for day-to-day communication and coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUR OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Natera™ is a global leader in cell-free DNA (cfDNA) testing, dedicated to oncology, women’s health, and organ health. Our aim is to make personalized genetic testing and diagnostics part of the standard of care to protect health and enable earlier and more targeted interventions that lead to longer, healthier lives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Natera team consists of highly dedicated statisticians, geneticists, doctors, laboratory scientists, business professionals, software engineers and many other professionals from world-class institutions, who care deeply for our work and each other. When you join Natera, you’ll work hard and grow quickly. Working alongside the elite of the industry, you’ll be stretched and challenged, and take pride in being part of a company that is changing the landscape of genetic disease management.&lt;/p&gt;
