&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Accountant&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Clinical Trials &amp;amp; R&amp;amp;D | Finance | Remote (US)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Natera is seeking an experienced and detail-oriented Senior Accountant to support key accounting operations related to Clinical Trials and Research &amp;amp; Development (R&amp;amp;D) activities. This role is responsible for clinical trial accruals, prepaid expense accounting, R&amp;amp;D expense analysis, month-end close activities, and financial reporting in compliance with GAAP, ASC 730, and SOX requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Accountant will partner closely with Clinical Operations, FP&amp;amp;A, Procurement, and external vendors including CROs and clinical sites to ensure accurate accounting and reporting of clinical trial and R&amp;amp;D expenditures. This individual will also support process improvements and technical accounting reviews related to clinical trial agreements and research activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a fully remote position, offering the opportunity to work from anywhere within the United States while collaborating with a high-performing and dynamic finance team. It is an excellent opportunity for an accounting professional looking to grow within a rapidly expanding public biotechnology company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical Trial &amp;amp; R&amp;amp;D Accounting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare monthly clinical trial accruals, prepaid roll-forwards, and reconciliations in accordance with ASC 730&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather enrollment, site activity, and milestone data from Clinical Operations to support accrual calculations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review CRO and clinical site invoices against contracted milestones and fee schedules; identify and investigate variances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support R&amp;amp;D expense accounting, including accruals, prepaid amortization, and cost allocations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with technical accounting reviews of new and amended clinical trial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain supporting schedules and documentation related to clinical trial and R&amp;amp;D accounting activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Clinical Operations, Legal, Procurement, and FP&amp;amp;A to ensure accurate and timely accounting treatment of research-related expenditures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Month-End Close &amp;amp; Financial Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform month-end close activities, including journal entries, account reconciliations, and flux analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare fluctuation analyses and provide explanations for financial trends and variances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, investigate, and correct accounting errors, inconsistencies, and reporting issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with GAAP, internal controls, and company accounting policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively communicate accounting, financial reporting, or control issues to management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audit requests, including preparation of supporting documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SOX Compliance &amp;amp; Process Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute SOX 404(b) controls related to clinical trial and R&amp;amp;D accounting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to process improvements across clinical trial and R&amp;amp;D accounting workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in automation, scalability, and operational efficiency initiatives within the accounting function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with team members to improve reporting accuracy and streamline month-end close processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 2–3 years of accounting or audit experience required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public accounting/audit background required; Big 4 experience strongly preferred given SOX and technical accounting scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in biotechnology, life sciences, healthcare, or pharmaceutical industries strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting R&amp;amp;D or clinical trial accounting activities preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
