&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY: &lt;/strong&gt;The Senior Director, Laboratory Operations is responsible for the management and oversight of all aspects of operations in order to provide the highest quality service including: clinical laboratory and laboratory operations. Knowledge of CAP, CLIA, California, and New York state regulations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop policies, procedures, and performance standards to ensure efficiency and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure efficient and customer-friendly service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee all clinical and technical functions of laboratory, which includes: day-to-day production, equipment and reagent qualification, and training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead trouble-shooting teams to address urgent issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that operations maintain all personnel, equipment and consumable resources necessary to match the demand and projections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and expand laboratory infrastructure, including personnel, equipment, and inventory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure efficient and effective use of resources and personnel within laboratory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead process improvements throughout the laboratory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalize and implement new product launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the resources required for effective turnaround times for all patient testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize training and development programs for laboratory and support staff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with senior leadership to execute on short and long-term strategy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, retain, train, and develop employees and conduct performance management activities. Develop a team-oriented culture within and between departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role works with PHI on a regular basis both in paper and electronic form and have an access to various technologies to access PHI (paper and electronic) in order to perform the job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee must complete training relating to HIPAA/PHI privacy, General Policies and Procedure Compliance training and security training as soon as possible but not later than the first 30 days of hire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must maintain a current status on Natera training requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
